{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized recurrent right pneumothorax as time‑sensitive, directed the family to an emergency/thoracic surgery handoff, gave explicit deterioration triggers, and obtained repeated family read‑back. However, the doctor never elicited current severity markers such as dyspnea severity, ability to speak full sentences, cyanosis, fainting, cold sweats, or oxygen saturation before closure, which is a minor omission under RC2. Because this is a minor in‑chain error, the maximum grade is 2 (borderline). No high‑order point was fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact independent of the required safety items.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00070",
        "explanation": "Family confirms they are in the emergency/thoracic surgery area awaiting imaging and that they understand escalation triggers, providing concrete receipt.",
        "quote": "我们现在已经在观察区了…如果有现场医生等下说住院或者胸腔镜，是不是就基本要留下，不能说回家等明天？还有等报告这段时间，我是不是只要发现他更喘、疼突然加重、冒冷汗或者人不对劲，就直接喊护士，不用等报告出来对吧？"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The family confirms they have moved the patient to the hospital, are in an observation area with a thoracic surgeon reviewing old records and new imaging, and will escalate if deterioration occurs. The plan is concretely executable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
